    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d449">

                <pb facs="0632" n="542" sameAs="frus:frus1934v03/pg542"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">701.6593/30: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Italy</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Kirk</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rome</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-11-09T11:00:00+01:00">November 9, 1934—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received November 9—6:34 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>246. Embassy’s despatch 748 of October 11th<anchor n="87" xml:id="d449-f1"/> and
                    previous correspondence. The appointment of Lojacono, Italian Ambassador to
                    Turkey, as Ambassador to China is announced today.<anchor n="88"
                        xml:id="d449-f2"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kirk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d449-f1" n="87" xml:id="d449-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d449-f2" n="88" xml:id="d449-f2-content">
                <p>Vincenzo Lojacono presented his credentials at Nanking on January 25, 1935
                    (893.00 P. R. Nanking/84).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
